    {
      "filename": "Plaque of Kamehameha May 8, 1819 Quote.jpg",
      "title": "File:Plaque of Kamehameha May 8, 1819 Quote.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/62/Plaque_of_Kamehameha_May_8%2C_1819_Quote.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plaque_of_Kamehameha_May_8,_1819_Quote.jpg",
      "width": 2816,
      "height": 2112,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "{{{1}}}",
      "description": "Pu'ukohola Heiau is all about King Kamehameha I, who united the Hawaiian Islands.  As far as teaching about Hawaiian history, I found the historic site to be incredibly informative. This plaque states: \"Endless is the good that I have given you to enjoy.\" Kamehameha I, May 8, 1819.",
